{< Nothing: the bottom sort — uninhabited type.
   No values of type Nothing exist.
   Bottom of the sort lattice: less(Nothing, ?T) for all T.
   Connected to denial rules: ⊥ in rule heads expresses non-existence. >}
sort anthill.prelude.Nothing
end

namespace anthill.prelude
  -- THE HOLE (WI-20261017-JRHZ0; kernel-language.md §5.4). `= todo()` is a body for
  -- any signature — `Nothing` conforms to every type — so an operation that is not
  -- written yet keeps its signature and still has something that runs it. Reaching
  -- it is a fault naming the running operation, the way Rust's `todo!()` and Scala's
  -- `???` are: no value, outside every effect row, caught by nothing. A program that
  -- holds one loads and runs; only a call that reaches it fails. Codegen refuses a
  -- body that calls it.
  operation todo() -> Nothing @[host_implemented]
end
